hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"136","We are Abu Husayn bin Ahmed bin Yunus, we are Anz, meaning Ibn al-Qasim, we are Husayn. H Ali bin Al-Mundhir and Harun bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Ali said: He said: Husayn bin Abd narrated to us The Most Gracious, and Aaron said: On the authority of Husayn. H. Bundar told us, Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Husayn. H Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi, Sufyan, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, told us on the authority of Mansour. H, Abu Musa told us, Abdul Rahman told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, Husayn, and Al-Amash. H and us Yusuf bin Musa, narrated by Waki’, narrated by Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, and Husayn, all of them on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “Peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he gets up at night to perform Tahajjud, he should cover his mouth with a siwak.” This is the wording of the hadith of Harun bin Ishaq. Abu Musa and Sa`id bin Abdul Rahman did not say: to recite the Tahajjud."
